The Subriach's Square is found as part of the Passion Facade in the highest church in the world - the Sagrada Familia, which is Barcelona.
The Passion Facade is facing west, towards the sunset, and represents the story of Jesus Christ's betrayal, death, and resurrection (his big story)
The part of the Subriach's Square that is on the Passion Facade depicts Judas and his betrayal.
The cool think about the Subriach's Square is that every row, column, and diagonal all add up to 33 which is how old he was when he died.
Another cool thing about the Sagrada Familia is that it was designed by this world famous archetect named Gaudi, who was dubbed and canonized as "God's Architect"

